Before changing product positioning, copy, information architecture, SEO entities, pricing language, or visual direction, read `.bolt/brand-identity.md` and preserve its current positioning.

Build production-ready pages, not generic templates. Levente Studio sells clear, professional websites and related growth/automation services for service businesses. Start with the customer's business problem and the website or workflow they need; measurement, automation and AI are supporting capabilities, not the headline.

Prefer human Hungarian copy, clear offers, real project proof, restrained premium design and a simple path to request a quote. Avoid unsupported guarantees, invented metrics, competitor-bashing, generic agency language and unnecessary English system jargon.

Use the shared offer data in `src/data/studio-offers.ts` instead of duplicating package names, prices or descriptions.

The current visual system is graphite + warm ivory + signal lime, with Inter for interface/body and Cormorant Garamond for editorial emphasis. Reuse the existing shared shell, CTA and card patterns instead of introducing parallel design generations.

This project uses Astro, React, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS and lucide-react. Prefer server-rendered/static content and existing dependencies. Hydrate client components only for real interactivity; tracking alone should use the shared data attributes/global handler.

Keep entity naming consistent: brand `Levente Studio`, person `Tarnóczi Levente`, role `weboldalkészítő és digitális rendszerépítő`.

Do not reintroduce legacy parallel Header, Contact, sticky CTA or diagnostic-console styles after this unification.


Revenue funnel rules:
- Every sales/content route must have a clear next step toward a relevant service, real proof, or the quote form.
- Preserve the true originating page when navigating to /kapcsolat/ so source_page remains useful for optimization.
- Audit/problem intent must not be automatically forced into a package. Inspect first, then recommend repair or rebuild.
- Prefer verified own-project proof before generic marketing claims. Never invent performance metrics.
- Keep the public primary CTA "Ajánlatot kérek"; phone and email are secondary channels.
